---
# Sample SHAPE — see
# ../insight-infra/mariadb-creds-sealedsecret.yaml.template for the
# workflow that generates a real, cluster-specific sealed manifest.
#
# `insight-keycloak-config` feeds the keycloak-config-cli hook Job
# (umbrella `keycloakConfig.existingSecret`, ADR-0003 broker realms as
# code). It is REQUIRED only when `keycloakConfig.enabled: true` in the
# umbrella values; the shipped local overlay leaves it off, so you can
# skip this Secret until the environment is migrated behind the broker.
#
# The Job consumes the whole Secret as environment variables, so it must
# carry BOTH kinds of keys:
#   - KEYCLOAK_USER / KEYCLOAK_PASSWORD — the config-cli admin login for
#     the Keycloak that `keycloakConfig.url` points at.
#   - One key per env-var placeholder the realm YAML under
#     ../../keycloak/realms/ references (client secrets, redirect URIs).
#     An unresolvable placeholder fails the import loudly.
#
# Stage the cleartext manifest in your password manager under
# `insight-local-insight-keycloak-config` before running `make seal-secret`.
apiVersion: bitnami.com/v1alpha1
kind: SealedSecret
metadata:
  name: insight-keycloak-config
  namespace: insight
spec:
  encryptedData:
    KEYCLOAK_USER:                        AgB...
    KEYCLOAK_PASSWORD:                    AgC...
    INSIGHT_AUTHENTICATOR_CLIENT_SECRET:  AgD...
    INSIGHT_AUTHENTICATOR_REDIRECT_URI:   AgE...
  template:
    metadata:
      name: insight-keycloak-config
      namespace: insight
    type: Opaque
